    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0648" n="622" xml:id="pg622"/>

                <head>310. Telegram From the Embassy in India to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d310-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>New Delhi</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-07-16T15:00:00+05:30">July 16, 1963, 3
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>246. Rangoon for Ambassador Bowles Only.
                        Embtel 245.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d310-f2"
                    /> Herewith full text of FonSec
                    Desai’s letter to me:</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Begin text</hi></p>
                <p>[This letter has not been declassified by the Indian Government.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Timmons</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, India,
                    General, 7/16/63-7/19/63. Secret; Operational Immediate; Limit Distribution.
                    Repeated to London and Rangoon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d310-f2" n="1" xml:id="d310-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 245 from New Delhi, July 16, Timmons reported that he had received a
                    letter from M.J. Desai indicating that
                    the Indian Government had decided to proceed with the proposed air defense
                    arrangements. (Department of State, Central Files, DEF 1-4 INDIA)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
